  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the same swipe actions in every list, with \"Annuler\" after Lu and the Super favori and Retirer swipes, so that lists behave alike.\n\n### Scope\n\nThe uniform swipe set of FEAT-008 (leading Lu with \"Annuler\", Super favori and Retirer swipes) in every list. LOT-125 keeps the legacy swipes (Lu, Supprimer) and the legacy context menu with page jumps.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: low · **M5** (UX evolution, operator decision 2026-11-02 on [#379](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379))\n- Split from LOT-125 (#216): the (b) half of the split in `docs/LOTS.md`. GAP ids: 028, 029, 034. UXD: UXD-08.\n- Legacy sources: none (this is an evolution, not a port); the (a) half cites the legacy code. Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-177-*.md`.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-125 (#216, done)\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the M5_OPEN decision: M5 opens after the M4 parity is validated, and the orchestrator opens it (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on #379). ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379#issuecomment-6573879240))\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] An optional evolution: the legacy UX stays the default, the change is a setting or a separate entry (UX principles of `docs/FEATURES.md`).\n- [ ] The spec has its \"Legacy counterpart\" and \"UX evolutions\" sections ([TEMPLATE](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/TEMPLATE.md)).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
